 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? That can be tough. Does he have any favorite foods? He might appreciate a vegetable stew with lentils, or pasta cooked with lot of water and drained at the last minute. No rush. No problem. Still here? Yes, I can. Your stepdad and you are going out to eat, right? Okay. Your stepdad's picky eater, and you want keep the bill down. Yes, we are. Order in for the two of you, and maybe a salad shared between you. For the entry, ask the waiter if they have a broiled or grilled vegetable side, or a light pasta with little sauce. Then stick your curry. Your stepdad might try the vegetable side, and your shared salad is low cost, low risk.",
